{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1010624-question-about-healing-times","id":1010624,"title":"Question about healing times...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-01T07:30:05-08:00","id":1010624,"title":"Question about healing times...","content":"Ok, order or operations question. For the following scenarios, assume no magic/supernatural effects at all, but sufficient medical attention as needed.<br /> <br /> Joe Q Mortal gets into a fight and takes 2 levels of bashing one round, a single level of lethal the next round and 2 more levels of bashing the 3rd round. 4th round, cops show up and the fight stops.<br /> <br /> Is Joe's Health Track like:<br /> / Bruised<br /> / Hurt<br /> X Injured<br /> / Wounded<br /> / Mauled<br /> <br /> Or is it like<br /> / Bruised<br /> / Hurt<br /> / Injured<br /> / Wounded<br /> X Mauled<br /> <br /> Or is it something entirely different?<br /> <br /> I ask because those two tracks have very different natural healing rates (1 week, 6 hours for the first option -vs.- 2 months, 4 hours for the second option).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 12-01-2016, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T07:37:30-08:00","id":1010628,"title":"","content":"Lethal damage pushes down bashing damage and aggravated damage pushes down lethal damage and bashing damage, so it would be Bruised X and everything down to Mauled /. So you would recover in two days or so.","s